data: {"type":"response.output_text.annotation.added","annotation":{"type":"url_citation","end_index":1365,"start_index":1353,"title":"NASA Mars Perseverance Rover Drives Marathon Runners Distance on Red ...","url":"https://www.spaceupclose.com/2026/07/nasa-mars-perseverance-rover-drives-marathon-runners-distance-on-red-planet-achieving-major-milestone-of-exploration/"},"annotation_index":2,"content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_09e2a1b7848791a6006a62a5d47eb0819783584c71a9f8c338","output_index":4,"sequence_number":334}

event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_09e2a1b7848791a6006a62a5d47eb0819783584c71a9f8c338","logprobs":[],"output_index":4,"sequence_number":335,"text":"The latest Mars Perseverance rover news includes two main updates:\n\n- **Perseverance has completed a “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reported that the rover reached **26.2 miles / 42.195 km** of driving on the Red Planet on **Sol 1890**, after about **five years and four months** of surface operations. That is much faster than Opportunity, which took over 11 years to reach the same distance. A Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter/HiRISE image captured the rover and its tracks shortly before the milestone, while Perseverance was operating west of Jezero Crater in an area nicknamed **“Arbot.”** 【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance is studying some of the oldest terrain yet examined by a Mars rover.** NASA/JPL says the rover has found evidence that a **245-foot / 75-meter stack of layered rocks** on Jezero Crater’s rim—called the **“Broom Point member”**—was likely built by repeated ancient asteroid impacts. These rocks may be **more than 3.9 billion years old**, offering a preserved record from a very early, violent period in solar system history. 【5:4†source】\n\n- **Its traverse continues beyond the marathon mark.** A later route update reported Perseverance at about **27.1 miles / 43.61 km** traveled as of mid-July 2026, continuing exploration west of Jezero after investigating the crater delta, Neretva Vallis, and climbing the crater rim in late 2024. 【5:1†source】"}

